  "body": "Auction: 34 Shortland Street, City on Wednesday 4 November 2026 at 10:00AM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nClose to St Heliers Beach, the village and an abundance of relaxing green spaces, this beautifully presented cedar and brick townhouse enjoys a superb position. Set well back from the road as one of just three homes in a private enclave, this thoughtfully configured, north-facing residence offers exceptional lock-and-leave convenience for retirees, professionals and busy families alike.\r\n\r\nThe refurbished interior seamlessly blends contemporary comfort with the character and generous proportions of its 1980s origins, across a spacious 227 sqm (approx.) two-level layout. A welcoming, light-filled entrance foyer features an elegant staircase ascending to a generous upper landing. From here, the spacious living room impresses with soaring vaulted ceilings, plantation shutters and an abundance of natural light. An adjoining dining area opens to a covered balcony, providing an inviting setting for alfresco dining and entertaining. The stylish, upgraded kitchen enjoys leafy green outlooks and features sleek tinted glass splashbacks, composite stone benchtops and modern appliances.\r\n\r\nAlso on this level is a guest powder room and the spacious main bedroom suite, complete with a beautifully appointed ensuite featuring a freestanding bath and dual-basin vanity. Downstairs, two generous bedrooms, both enjoying seamless outdoor access, are serviced by a second family bathroom and separate laundry with exterior access. Outdoors, a sheltered barbecue patio nestled beneath the balcony is framed by nikau palms, Japanese maples and lush established planting, creating a peaceful, resort-like retreat ideal for entertaining or simply unwinding.\r\n\r\nDouble internal-access garaging is complemented by a substantial adjoining carport, all positioned on a beautifully landscaped 337 sqm (approx.) site. Designed for effortless living, the low-maintenance grounds mean there are no lawns to mow, leaving more time to enjoy everything this exceptional location has to offer.\r\n\r\nAn easy, flat stroll takes you to St Heliers Village and Beach, with its boutique shops, popular cafés, restaurants and bars. Nearby recreational attractions include bowling and tennis clubs, Vellenoweth Green, Dingle Dell and Madills Farm Reserves. Zoned for St Heliers School, St Ignatius School and Glendowie College, this is an outstanding opportunity to secure a beautifully presented, easy-care home in the heart of the Bays.\r\n\r\nSee interactive features for this property on barfoot.co.nz. Click the \"View office website\" link at the bottom of this page.",
